            "review_title": "Review at Banh Beo Hue Thanh Nga",
            "review_text": "Jon K\n11 contributions\n0\nHue food, a gem in Ho Chi Minh City\nJan 2017 • Family\nIf you can’t go to the city of Hue for their traditional food, then you don’t need to leave Ho Chi Minh City. Me and my family had the pleasure of dining at this establishment. We learned that the owner of the restaurant had originally came from Hue. So, the food is truly authentic and you can get Hue food all in one place. \n\nWe were served a seven-course meal, and each dish was aesthetically pleasing. Additionally, the food was fresh, very tasty, and we were filled by the end. To finish off, we had flan made with coffee, which was extraordinary. Overall experience was spectacular and all the food was savory. By far it’s the best food I have had yet. I highly recommend this place.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 21, 2017",
